SUMMARY:FOREIGN MATERIAL – Matt Castellvi & Ibrahim Al Hajjaj
LOCATION:Comedy Cafe Amsterdam\, Amsterdam
DESCRIPTION:FOREIGN MATERIAL is Matt Castellvi’s brand-new stand-up show 
 about dating\, bad decisions\, getting older\, living abroad\, and trying t
 o behave like an adult while repeatedly proving he probably shouldn’t be 
 trusted with that responsibility.\n\\n\nExpect brutally honest stories\, ch
 aotic dating experiences\, cultural misunderstandings\, dark thoughts\, cro
 wd work\, and the kind of jokes that make you laugh first and reconsider yo
 ur life choices second. It’s messy\, personal\, fast\, and still being bu
 ilt live — which means anything can happen\, and the funniest part of the
  night might be something nobody planned.\n\\n\nCastellvi is a former Boom 
 Chicago cast member who has performed internationally for more than 20 year
 s\, appeared at the Edinburgh and Adelaide Fringe festivals\, and opened fo
 r comedians including Iliza Shlesinger\, Nate Bargatze\, Jim Gaffigan\, Jos
 h Johnson\, TJ Miller and Jeff Arcuri.\n\\n\nJoining him is Saudi actor and
  comedian Ibrahim Al Hajjaj\, star of the hit comedy Sattar and winner of t
 he 2023 Joy Award for Favorite Actor.\n\\n\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.
